dist/

# Belt and braces (G2 / A-WS3.1). package.json carries a `files` allowlist,
# which supersedes this. But npm's fallback path reads THIS file, never the
# repo root's. This package is destined for the public repo, so the backstop
# matters: if the allowlist is ever removed, this keeps an env file out of a pack.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
